Seven Apple stores across France are <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/21/apple-stores-looted-during-french-protests/">closed on</a> today, as the country prepares for another round of demonstrations a week after looters targeted two of the company's locations.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/Apple-Champs-Elysees-Paris-France.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072650" /><br/>
As first spotted by <a href="https://www.macg.co/aapl/2026/10/manifestations-plusieurs-apple-store-fermes-ce-samedi-311803"><em>MacGeneration</em></a>, the affected stores include all three Paris locations: <a href="https://www.apple.com/fr/retail/champs-elysees/">Champs-Élysées</a>, <a href="https://www.apple.com/fr/retail/opera/">Opéra</a>, and <a href="https://www.apple.com/fr/retail/marchesaintgermain/">Marché Saint-Germain</a>. Apple's website also lists Saturday closures for <a href="https://www.apple.com/fr/retail/sainte-catherine/">Bordeaux Sainte-Catherine</a>, <a href="https://www.apple.com/fr/retail/lille/">Lille</a>, <a href="https://www.apple.com/fr/retail/strasbourg/">Strasbourg</a>, and <a href="https://www.apple.com/fr/retail/aix-en-provence/">Aix-en-Provence</a>.<br/>
<br/>
The closures are likely a precaution to protect employees and stores during the protests. The seven locations have entrances directly onto the street, while Apple's stores inside shopping malls are expected to operate normally during the period.<br/>
<br/>
Apple's Lille and Bordeaux stores were looted during the unrest on October 17 unrest. Both were among many businesses targeted across France.<br/>
<br/>
The demonstrations concern rising living costs and poor conditions in schools, according to <a href="https://apnews.com/article/ca52b503a4ac8b2a489109f7de852847">the <em>Associated Press</em></a>. Hundreds of thousands are said to have protested peacefully on October 17, but violence and looting broke out in several cities.<br/>
<br/>
Following the looting, <a href="https://iphoneaddict.fr/post/news-437920-lapple-store-lille-reste-ferme-apres-pillages-17-octobre">reports emerged</a> of stolen iPhones displaying warnings that they had been disabled and were being tracked, along with instructions to return them to their stores of origin. A <a href="https://x.com/LesignalFr/status/2111778835884863673">video shared by Le Signal</a> purportedly shows the message.<br/>
<br/>
